 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "The reference rate is the official daily benchmark spot rate of the rupee, quoted as rupees per unit of foreign currency (INR per 1 USD; INR per 1 EUR). The Reserve Bank of India compiled and published it on Mumbai business days until 9 July 2018; since 10 July 2018 the benchmark has been computed and disseminated by Financial Benchmarks India Pvt. Ltd. (FBIL), an RBI-recognised benchmark administrator, and RBI reproduces the FBIL rates in the Weekly Statistical Supplement ('Ratios and Rates' table, rows 'INR-US$ Spot Rate' and 'INR-Euro Spot Rate'). FBIL's USD/INR rate is a volume-weighted average of actual spot USD/INR transactions on the Refinitiv and CCIL electronic trading platforms within a randomly selected 15-minute window between 11:30 and 12:30 hours, with trades beyond ±3 standard deviations excluded; the EUR/INR cross rate is derived by crossing that USD/INR rate with EUR/USD.",
   "source_name": "Financial Benchmarks India Pvt. Ltd. (FBIL) — Reference Rate (RBI-recognised benchmark administrator)",
   "source_url": "https://www.fbil.org.in/securities?mq=o&op=referencerate",
   "term": "USD/INR and EUR/INR spot exchange rates (Reference Rate)"
